This artifact also contains small pieces of third-party or externally derived material with the following provenance:

- `ref/fips202.c` is based on public-domain Keccak/FIPS202 implementations: Ronny Van Keer's `crypto_hash/keccakc512/simple/` implementation from SUPERCOP and the public-domain TweetFips202 implementation by Gilles Van Assche, Daniel J. Bernstein, and Peter Schwabe.
- `avx2/f1600x4.S` notes that it was taken from Bas Westerbaan's 4-way SHAKE implementation for SPHINCS+ and adapted to use Keccak Code Package byte-rotation style.
- `avx512/keccakf1600x8.c`, `avx512/fips202x8.c`, and `avx512/fips202x8.h` are derived from the eXtended Keccak Code Package (XKCP), specifically the 8-way AVX-512 Keccak-f[1600] code path. XKCP's Keccak implementations are marked CC0/public domain upstream.
- `third_party/*.txt` records upstream revisions used for benchmark comparison, and `third_party/*.patch` contains small local benchmark harness patches for those upstream projects. Those upstream projects retain their own licenses and are not vendored as part of the core Lithium-Code implementation; `external/` checkouts created by reproduction scripts are gitignored and are not part of the submitted artifact.

If this artifact is redistributed with generated `external/` checkouts or third-party benchmark source trees, keep the corresponding upstream license files from those projects with the redistributed copy.

Subsequent Copa adapters share the tagged scalar scheme and add local vector
NTT/CRT, Q63, polynomial and XOF hooks. The Keccak wrappers replace typed
double output stores with unaligned integer stores and copy exact short
input tails, fixing sanitizer alignment reports and input overreads without
changing the default KAT bytes.

The SIMD signers additionally expose an attempt counter only when compiled
with BENCH_COUNT_ATTEMPTS for the shared cycle benchmark. Ordinary builds
exclude the counter and retain their default LITHIUM KAT behavior.
